# Phase 1 requires NO environment variables. The app is fully local-first.
#
# Phase 2 (optional Supabase sync). Only PUBLIC values may ever be exposed client-side.
# Never put a service-role key in any NEXT_PUBLIC_ variable or in the frontend.
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_URL=
# NEXT_PUBLIC_SUPABASE_ANON_KEY=

# Yahoo Fantasy API (feasibility spike, docs/YAHOO_API.md). SERVER-SIDE ONLY.
# Never prefix any of these with NEXT_PUBLIC_. Put real values in .env.local (git-ignored) or in
# Vercel project environment variables — never in the repository.
# YAHOO_CLIENT_ID=
# YAHOO_CLIENT_SECRET=
# Must exactly match the redirect URI registered with the Yahoo app (https://… or "oob").
# YAHOO_REDIRECT_URI=
# 32+ random bytes, hex or base64 (e.g. `openssl rand -hex 32`). Signs the OAuth state.
# YAHOO_STATE_SECRET=
# Exactly 32 random bytes, hex or base64 (`openssl rand -hex 32`). Encrypts the stored token set.
# YAHOO_TOKEN_ENCRYPTION_KEY=
